Z||000005||isthiswhereiputausername?||12-27-2001||08:57 PM||||Ouch. after reading this Sour Lemon, I thought I should post a warning.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sour Lemon:<BR><B>My 2 cats.<BR>Georgina is a one year old kitty who enjoys playing with anything stringy.  She steals the laces from my shoes at least once a week.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Be careful with her.. Cats love string but they cant digest it at all.  String tends to "wrap" around their stomachs and would need surgery to remove.. <P>Also.. If you ever see a piece of string while they are using the litterbox..NEVER pull it out(believe me,some do) keep an eye on it and cut it with scissors.. (pulling it could cut their intestines.)<P>Cats are sometimes TOO curious for their own good.. you almost need to "baby proof" your house..<P>Same as tinsel and garland from Christmas trees, we dont use it anymore on our trees or anything..<P><BR>PS we have 5 indoor cats  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
